sentences.l:
and kindled for her a fire
an old woman of Apeire, chamber-attendant Eurymedusa,
whom once from Apeire ships brought, both-sides-curving;

the one, having no son, struck silver-bowed Apollo,
a bridegroom, in his hall, one only daughter having left,
Arete;

As much as the Phaeacians beyond all men are skilled
to drive a swift ship on the open-sea, so the women
are craftswomen of looms;
